---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/landing.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="The graph that makes your agent finish faster">

<div class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>The graph that makes your<br><span class="accent">agent finish faster</span></h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Embedded code-graph engine for AI code assistants. One Rust daemon per repo extracts dependencies via Tree-sitter, serves blast radius with source inline. Your agent acts in turn 1, not turn 15.</p>
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <img src={`${base}/favicon.svg`} alt="" width="36" height="36" />
      <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text-primary);">Graphite</span>
    </div>
    <a href="https://github.com/daviguides/graphite" class="hero-cta">View on GitHub</a>
    <p class="hero-links">Rust &middot; Single binary &middot; CozoDB + in-memory adjacency &middot; <a href={`${base}/docs/architecture`}>Docs</a></p>

    <div class="graph-hero" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 700 320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <line class="edge" x1="350" y1="80" x2="220" y2="160"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="350" y1="80" x2="480" y2="160"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="220" y1="160" x2="140" y2="240"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="220" y1="160" x2="280" y2="240"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="480" y1="160" x2="420" y2="240"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="480" y1="160" x2="560" y2="240"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="140" y1="240" x2="80" y2="300"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="280" y1="240" x2="340" y2="300"/>
        <line class="edge" x1="560" y1="240" x2="620" y2="300"/>
        <line class="edge-blast" x1="350" y1="80" x2="220" y2="160" id="b1"/>
        <line class="edge-blast" x1="350" y1="80" x2="480" y2="160" id="b2"/>
        <line class="edge-blast" x1="220" y1="160" x2="140" y2="240" id="b3"/>
        <line class="edge-blast" x1="220" y1="160" x2="280" y2="240" id="b4"/>
        <line class="edge-blast" x1="480" y1="160" x2="420" y2="240" id="b5"/>
        <line class="edge-blast" x1="480" y1="160" x2="560" y2="240" id="b6"/>
        <circle class="node-active" cx="350" cy="80" r="8" id="n0"/>
        <circle class="node-blast" cx="220" cy="160" r="6" id="n1"/>
        <circle class="node-blast" cx="480" cy="160" r="6" id="n2"/>
        <circle class="node-blast" cx="140" cy="240" r="6" id="n3"/>
        <circle class="node-blast" cx="280" cy="240" r="6" id="n4"/>
        <circle class="node-blast" cx="420" cy="240" r="6" id="n5"/>
        <circle class="node-blast" cx="560" cy="240" r="6" id="n6"/>
        <circle class="node" cx="80" cy="300" r="5"/>
        <circle class="node" cx="340" cy="300" r="5"/>
        <circle class="node" cx="620" cy="300" r="5"/>
        <text class="node-label" x="350" y="65" text-anchor="middle">changed_fn()</text>
        <text class="node-label" x="220" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0" id="l1">caller_a</text>
        <text class="node-label" x="480" y="150" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0" id="l2">caller_b</text>
        <text class="node-label" x="140" y="232" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0" id="l3">handler</text>
        <text class="node-label" x="280" y="232" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0" id="l4">test_a</text>
        <text class="node-label" x="420" y="232" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0" id="l5">service</text>
        <text class="node-label" x="560" y="232" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0" id="l6">api_route</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="landing-section fade-in">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">The problem</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Your agent explores when it should be acting</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">AI code assistants spend most of their turns reading files to understand architecture. Each file read is a tool call, each tool call is latency, each wrong file is a wasted turn.</p>
    <div class="pain-grid">
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="number">30</div>
        <h3>Files read per task</h3>
        <p>The agent reads dozens of files to map dependencies before making a single edit. Most of those reads discover things the graph already knows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="number">60%</div>
        <h3>Time spent exploring</h3>
        <p>Exploration dominates execution. The agent's first edit often comes after 5+ tool calls of pure discovery. Every session re-discovers the same codebase.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="number">0</div>
        <h3>Persistent context</h3>
        <p>Understanding dies with the session. No queryable graph, no dependency index, no blast radius. Every new conversation starts blind.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="landing-section fade-in">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">Measured</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Real tasks, real repo, real numbers</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Effectiveness benchmark on a production multi-language repo (Python, TypeScript, Rust; 50K+ lines). Same model, same tasks, multiple repeats. Interception hooks deliver graph context transparently.</p>
    <div class="evidence-grid">
      <div class="evidence-card without">
        <h4>Without Graphite</h4>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value">14.5</div><div class="label">median turns per task</div></div>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value">89.8s</div><div class="label">median wall-clock</div></div>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value">6.5</div><div class="label">files read per task</div></div>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value">7.0</div><div class="label">calls before first edit</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-card with-graphite">
        <h4>With Graphite</h4>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value" style="color: var(--color-accent)">11.5</div><div class="label">median turns per task</div></div>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value" style="color: var(--color-accent)">68.7s</div><div class="label">median wall-clock</div></div>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value" style="color: var(--color-accent)">3.0</div><div class="label">files read per task</div></div>
        <div class="metric"><div class="value" style="color: var(--color-accent)">5.0</div><div class="label">calls before first edit</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="evidence-note">Pilot C2 vs A2 on issue-form tasks (hard/medium difficulty, cross-module). Hook latency median 27ms. Full methodology in <a href={`${base}/docs/benchmarks`}>benchmarks</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="landing-section fade-in">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">How it works</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Extract, persist, serve</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">One daemon per repo keeps the graph always hot. Every agent session queries the same indexed graph through a local socket.</p>
    <div class="mechanism-steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">01</div>
        <h3>Extract</h3>
        <p>Tree-sitter parses source code into symbols, calls, imports, inheritance. Python today; Rust and TypeScript next. Deterministic IDs, edge confidence tags.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">02</div>
        <h3>Persist</h3>
        <p>CozoDB (embedded Datalog) holds facts and derives confidence by rule. In-memory adjacency serves traversals in microseconds. Atomic per-file updates; reads never wait for writes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">03</div>
        <h3>Serve</h3>
        <p>CLI, MCP shim, and interception hooks deliver blast radius, source inline, covering tests. The agent gets the answer and the code in one call.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="landing-section fade-in">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">In practice</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">What the agent sees</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Interception hooks rewrite the agent's grep into an enriched graph-aware answer. The agent gets structural context without changing its habits.</p>
    <div class="cli-demo">
      <div class="cli-header">
        <span class="cli-dot"></span><span class="cli-dot"></span><span class="cli-dot"></span>
        <span class="cli-title">terminal</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="cli-body" is:raw><span class="cli-prompt">$</span> <span class="cli-highlight">graphite blast rebase_onto_base</span>

<span class="cli-comment"># Blast radius: 4 symbols in 3 files (depth 3, trusted edges only)</span>
<span class="cli-comment"># Confidence: 3 EXTRACTED, 1 INFERRED (resolved)</span>

<span class="cli-confidence-e">EXTRACTED</span>  rover/git_ops.py:142    <span class="cli-highlight">rebase_onto_base()</span>
  <span class="cli-output">  def rebase_onto_base(repo_path, base_branch, ...):</span>
  <span class="cli-output">      """Rebase current worktree onto the given base branch."""</span>

<span class="cli-confidence-e">EXTRACTED</span>  rover/git_ops.py:198    <span class="cli-highlight">rebase_main_onto_current()</span>
  <span class="cli-output">  calls rebase_onto_base (depth 1)</span>

<span class="cli-confidence-e">EXTRACTED</span>  runner/engine.py:87     <span class="cli-highlight">pre_hook()</span>
  <span class="cli-output">  calls rebase_main_onto_current (depth 2)</span>

<span class="cli-confidence-i">INFERRED</span>   runner/engine.py:245    <span class="cli-highlight">execute_task()</span>
  <span class="cli-output">  calls pre_hook (depth 3, resolved via call chain)</span>

<span class="cli-comment"># Covering tests: tests/test_rover.py, tests/test_engine.py</span>
<span class="cli-comment"># graph_rev: 1847  stale: false  latency: 0.4ms</span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="landing-section fade-in">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">Honesty built in</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">The agent knows when to trust the graph</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Every edge carries a confidence tier and provenance. Responses disclose when a result is a lower bound and why. Assertiveness from transparency, not from hiding uncertainty.</p>
    <div class="confidence-demo">
      <div class="confidence-tier extracted">
        <div class="tier-label">EXTRACTED</div>
        <div class="tier-line"></div>
        <p>Parsed directly from source. Static call, explicit import, type annotation. The graph saw it in the AST.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="confidence-tier inferred">
        <div class="tier-label">INFERRED</div>
        <div class="tier-line"></div>
        <p>Derived by rule. Duck-typed call resolved to a likely target. Marked with provenance so the agent can verify if needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="confidence-tier ambiguous">
        <div class="tier-label">AMBIGUOUS</div>
        <div class="tier-line"></div>
        <p>Multiple possible targets. Dynamic dispatch, reflection, generated code. The graph says "I don't know which one" instead of guessing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="landing-section fade-in">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">Under the hood</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Hybrid engine, measured</h2>
