        <text x="560" y="421" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-sans)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-text-secondary)">bridge</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="arch-features">
      <div class="arch-feature">
        <h4>Always-hot graph</h4>
        <p>File watcher indexes eagerly. Queries hit an already-indexed graph. At most a short freshness barrier, never a rebuild.</p>
        <div class="perf">mtime check + BLAKE3 per file</div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-feature">
        <h4>Microsecond traversals</h4>
        <p>In-memory adjacency serves blast radius in plain Rust BFS. CozoDB handles facts, rules, and search.</p>
        <div class="perf">19-80 µs on worst real hub</div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-feature">
        <h4>Source inline</h4>
        <p>Responses return verbatim source with line numbers alongside graph context. One call = dependency context + actual code.</p>
        <div class="perf">Zero follow-up file reads</div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-feature">
        <h4>Single binary</h4>
        <p>Tree-sitter grammars, CozoDB, daemon, clients, file watcher. One Rust executable. No runtime, no npm, no venv.</p>
        <div class="perf">~7K lines of Rust</div>
      </div>
    </div>
